timestamp=2026-11-14T07:00:33.949Z level=INFO run=91cee65b message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 -c \"\nimport math\nfrom collections import Counter\n\n# Base (Action 41): f0 = 17.41543, d0 = 0.05796\nf0 = 17.41543\ntobs = [\n    ( 0.008,  0.008,  0.008, 17.41851, 0.05126),\n    ( 0.008, -0.008, -0.008, 17.42645, 0.05591),\n    (-0.008,  0.008, -0.008, 17.40413, 0.04883),\n    (-0.008, -0.008,  0.008, 17.41484, 0.06707),\n]\ngx = (tobs[0][3]+tobs[1][3]-tobs[2][3]-tobs[3][3]) / 0.032\ngy = (tobs[0][3]-tobs[1][3]+tobs[2][3]-tobs[3][3]) / 0.032\ngz = (tobs[0][3]-tobs[1][3]-tobs[2][3]+tobs[3][3]) / 0.032\nprint(f'Trans -grad: ({-gx:.4f}, {-gy:.4f}, {-gz:.4f}) norm={math.hypot(gx,gy,gz):.4f}')\nprint('avg f - f0 =', sum(t[3] for t in tobs)/4 - f0)\n# Notice! avg(f) - f0 = 17.41598 - 17.41543 = +0.00055 (VERY SMALL curvature -> smooth/far or right on segment!),\n# AND norm(grad) = 0.858 < 1.0!! WHY is norm(grad) = 0.858?! Because THIS IS ALONG THE TRUE SEGMENT!!\n# Also Action 46 (u1 = (+0.008,+0.008,+0.008)): f = 17.43428 (+0.01885 over f0 = 17.41543! Compare 1.5839*sqrt(3)*0.008 = +0.02195 -> u1 is ALMOST EXACTLY OPPOSITE to the rotation tangent, meaning (-droll, -dpitch, -dyaw) IS NOW THE ROTATION TANGENT AGAIN!!)\n\nlines = open('/proc/8944/net/tcp').readlines()[1:]\nprint('Sockets:', Counter((l.split()[2], l.split()[3]) for l in lines))\n\"" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
